  - type: metin
    baslik: Where does the parent fit in?
    metin: |-
      In child therapy a parent is not an observer. You are the person who builds your child's daily life, so what changes at home often matters more than what changes in the session. This is why parent sessions happen at intervals; when sibling relationships or tension between partners comes to the fore, [family therapy](/en/services/family-therapy.html) may also come into the picture.

      What the child shares is handled with care for their privacy when it is discussed with parents. At our centre, sessions and your personal information are protected in line with confidentiality principles.
